son\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e073f07ef928f6e75ebef5b72a222bc46f19d8473e0e355814a3d99164fe7668","event_uuid":"a9a893f0-5179-46ab-9c5b-e6be1eaab3d7","position":{"commit_sha":"cbf6234f7b71f011a6581fe0cb5b71c0e8a577d4","position":"1787353041308343001-a9a893f0-5179-46ab-9c5b-e6be1eaab3d7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"env_integration","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Observed AGAIN 2026-08-21, during unrelated work (f1bc outbound_differ split). New details beyond the description:\n\n- Reproduced on a DIFFERENT base sha than the ticket records: the description cites failure at pristine main 6fb4d801c9; this observation is on origin/main e016c152794b (post-S2 438a merge), in worktree /Users/joeoakhart/impl-mapping-seam. Confirms the failure is base-independent / environmental, not tied to a specific main revision.\n- Interpreter: cpython-3.12.13-macos-aarch64 (uv-managed .venv), macOS (APFS temp dir /private/var/folders/...).\n- This run's exact failure: git -C <tmp>/pytest-19493/test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_t0/bare.git cat-file -t 1d849b8b8c00f78552f75b68c66ed3a9eac20bdb returned exit 128 (object absent from the bare remote after push) — same mechanism as described, fresh SHA/tmp path each run.\n- Blast radius confirmed isolated: pytest -x stopped ONLY at this test (1764 passed before it); deselecting just this one test → 3036 passed, 1 deselected across tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py + tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/. No collateral failures, so the standing 'ignore only this test' guidance remains safe.\n- Still deterministic in this env (fails every run). No retry/skip applied — deselected only for local validation of the unrelated refactor, per the ignore-this-one guidance.","timestamp":1787347012508543001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 (rebar-debug) COMPLETE — root cause confirmed with a cited mechanism.\n\nMECHANISM: This host's agent harness injects git config via environment: GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=2, GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=safe.bareRepository, GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=explicit (plus credential.interactive=never). Under safe.bareRepository=explicit (git >= 2.38 security policy), git refuses IMPLICIT discovery of a bare repository: any 'git -C <bare.git> <cmd>' exits 128 with \"fatal: cannot use bare repository '<path>' (safe.bareRepository is 'explicit')\". Explicit naming via 'git --git-dir <bare.git>' is always permitted, as are push/fetch/clone against the bare path.\n\nWHY THIS TEST: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py's _git() helper (line ~57) runs ['git', '-C', str(repo), ...]; test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote passes the BARE fixture repo to it (cat-file -t at line 215, rev-parse at line 217). The push succeeds (the object IS in the bare remote — earlier 'object absent' diagnoses were wrong); the verification command itself is refused. Reproduced deterministically in a scratch dir: 'git -C bare.git cat-file -t <oid>' → 128 with the exact fatal above; 'git --git-dir bare.git cat-file -t <oid>' → 'blob', exit 0; the same oid resolves via rev-parse. This also explains why prior sessions saw it as env-specific: only hosts whose harness injects the explicit policy fail.\n\nDEFECT CLASSIFICATION: a REAL test-portability defect, not purely environmental. The repo's own contract says bare-repo fixtures must survive safe.bareRepository=explicit: tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py enforces exactly this policy for other fixtures, and prior art (tests/_git_upkeep.py::_git, test_concurrency_regression.py::_bare_git) already uses 'git --git-dir' for bare remotes. test_ref_lock.py predates/misses that pattern.\n\nFIX (Phase 2, strict RED→GREEN): route bare-repo git invocations in test_ref_lock.py through explicit --git-dir naming (matching the _git_upkeep prior art) so the test passes under both the default and the explicit safe.bareRepository policy. RED = test fails under injected explicit policy (reproduced now); GREEN = passes under both explicit and devnull-global policies, 5x locally, full reconciler suite green. Production _ref_lock code is NOT implicated — it never runs git inside a bare repo via -C.","timestamp":1787349386081296001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RESOLVED. Fix merged to main as 1ab54b3042 via Gerrit change 2028 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2028), LLM-Review +1 (rebar review bot) + Verified +1 (rebar CI bot), submitted with all CI matrix jobs green including pytest on macos-latest.\n\nChange: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py adds a _bare_git helper using explicit 'git --git-dir <bare.git>' naming (the _git_upkeep prior-art pattern) and routes the AC0 test's two bare-remote inspections (cat-file -t, rev-parse) through it; work-tree repos keep 'git -C'. No production code changed.\n\nAcceptance criteria verified:\n- Root cause with cited mechanism: recorded in the previous comment (safe.bareRepository=explicit injected via GIT_CONFIG_* refuses implicit discovery of bare repos → git -C exit 128; --git-dir permitted).\n- Test passes in this environment: 5x consecutive passes under the ambient explicit policy, plus the whole module under GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 (default policy) — both postures green, mirroring test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py.\n- Full reconciler suite green: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/ 3032 passed, 0 failed (plus the module re-run green on merged main).\n\nStanding 'ignore only this test' guidance is now obsolete — the test is portable to hosts that inject the explicit bare-repo policy.","timestamp":1787352246639389001}],"created_at":1787336921704316001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d12a7ae4-8bf2-463a-b6be-2ba9a614bd3d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b9b4-f460-2d54-4872"},{"link_uuid":"5b3b26eb-7b35-4ad1-b10f-84e2dd884eec","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0831-a2c4-e3ec-4656"},{"link_uuid":"a9a893f0-5179-46ab-9c5b-e6be1eaab3d7","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"524d-00fa-66ef-4432"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote` fails deterministically (exit 128 from `git -C <tmp>/bare.git cat-file -t <oid>`) on any host whose environment injects `safe.bareRepository=explicit` — as this macOS agent harness does via `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0/GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0`. At least six prior closed tickets re-diagnosed the same failure as 'known-unrelated'; every session pays that cost again.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed, see comments): under git's `safe.bareRepository=explicit` security policy, `git -C <bare.git>` uses implicit repository discovery, which git refuses for bare repos (`fatal: cannot use bare repository … (safe.bareRepository is 'explicit')`). The push actually succeeds — the object IS in the bare remote — but the test's verification helper `_git()` runs `git -C` against the bare fixture and is refused. Explicit naming via `git --git-dir` is always permitted. The repo already treats this as a portability contract: `tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py` asserts bare-repo fixtures survive the explicit policy, and `tests/_git_upkeep.py` / `test_concurrency_regression.py::_bare_git` already use `--git-dir`. `test_ref_lock.py` misses that established pattern — a test-portability defect, not a product bug (production `_ref_lock` never runs `git -C` inside a bare repo).\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the class in the test module: give `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py` a bare-repo-safe git helper that addresses the bare fixture with explicit `--git-dir` naming (matching the `_git_upkeep` prior art) instead of `git -C`, and route the AC0 test's bare-remote inspections (cat-file, rev-parse) through it. Work-tree repos keep `-C`. No production code changes; no retry/skip.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py` (only file).\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN on the existing test itself: it currently fails under the injected `safe.bareRepository=explicit` policy (reproduced deterministically) and must pass after the fix under BOTH postures — the ambient explicit policy and a devnull-global default policy — mirroring the two-posture check in `test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py`. Verify 5x locally plus the full reconciler unit suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Root cause identified with a cited mechanism (recorded on this ticket).\n- [x] `test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote` passes in this environment (ambient `safe.bareRepository=explicit`) and under the default policy — verified by running the test 5x locally.\n- [x] Full reconciler suite green afterwards.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_ref_lock.py","reason":"route bare-repo git inspections through explicit --git-dir naming so the test survives safe.bareRepository=explicit"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0831-a2c4-e3ec-4656"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"186a2494-e336-4dda-b6c6-827bdbbe21da","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"02e8-96bd-82c1-45ff","ticket_type":"bug","title":"state/test_ref_lock.py::test_ac0_blob_ref_roundtrips_through_remote fails on pristine main in local macOS env (git cat-file 128)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["314a53b3-765f-4b8b-824a-b86aa2e4c614","06210a5e-2c71-4eae-aa84-26d66eeca0c7","8e68e237-c55e-4de8-a3bc-d839f1d11ffd","36c4d131-9dbd-45d0-b324-e9067e2522f2","3090125d-ba00-406f-8f8a-fadbe80627a8","1ef441f0-aca1-4cb2-ada5-e7ca4e8cb741","d0927e4b-6339-49ff-afe5-0c4d7d9fede0","5b3b26eb-7b35-4ad1-b10f-84e2dd884eec","42a3e13b-42ce-4ff1-a193-0d084b103c70","6d4368f2-fe63-4959-b39b-0d6b9048073b","186a2494-e336-4dda-b6c6-827bdbbe21da","e0be8f6d-8a2f-4dfe-9975-ad3706b39e4b","a9a893f0-5179-46ab-9c5b-e6be1eaab3d7"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787355502957829001,"uuid":"f27c8f5d-6343-4b08-94e6-f0007dd9fad1"}